-- title:
--   Is Proj Unitary Conj
-- statement:
--   **Unitary conjugation preserves projectivity.** Let `P` be a projector and `U` a unitary matrix on the same finite space. Conjugating `P` by `U` produces another self-adjoint idempotent:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{IsProj}(P)
--   \Longrightarrow
--   \operatorname{IsProj}(U^{\dagger}PU),
--   \qquad (U^{\dagger}PU)^2=U^{\dagger}PU.
--   $$
--
--   This is the algebraic closure property needed to transport projectors through the isometries and basis changes in projectivization constructions.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.isProj_unitary_conj`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
